  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 202cb6532a4a7f80682b508098ca96f0, type: 3}
  m_Name: item_l35_frame_protocol
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::GlorifiedBody.Interaction.ItemDefinition
  itemId: l35_frame_protocol
  displayName: A RECORDER
  kind: 6
  drugType: 0
  colour: {r: 0.95, g: 0.55, b: 0.2, a: 1}
  description: A recording. It plays while she walks. A fight pauses it.
  logText: 'Okay. Frame protocol, the upright restraint in the Hold. Listen to this
    before your first shift, not after.


    One. The line stays in. It feeds the
    filter, the filter takes the tincture out of her blood, and while that''s running
    she can''t do anything, and I mean anything, she''s a patient while it runs,
    that''s all she is.


    Two. The cage stays on the Crown, grounded to the frame.
    You find it off, it goes back on before you do one other thing.


    Three.
    Never alone. Two in the box, two in the guard post, I don''t care if it''s Christmas.


    Four.
    The line comes out, you don''t put it back. The Hold seals itself, the tube pulls
    away, the doors lock, and you get behind a door and you wait for it to come back
    for you.


    That''s for her as much as it''s for you. Nobody''s ever had to
    do that last part. Listen to it anyway.'
  readFlag: 
  mapFloor: 
